WEBVTT

00:01.935 --> 00:04.699
<i>NARRATOR: In the television comedy
world, the people are entertained...</i>

00:04.804 --> 00:07.500
<i>by two separate yet equally important
types of shows.</i>

00:07.607 --> 00:10.508
<i>Traditional sitcoms that get laughs out
of everyday situations...</i>

00:10.610 --> 00:14.376
<i>like trying to fix your own plumbing
or inviting two dates to the same dance.</i>

00:14.481 --> 00:18.008
<i>And animated shows that make jokes
about farting. This is the latter.</i>

00:20.787 --> 00:22.254
Sorry. I just farted.

00:23.857 --> 00:25.688
[Law & Order theme song]

00:55.121 --> 00:56.952
I'm glad you guys could come tonight.

00:57.057 --> 01:00.151
Chris, honey, we wouldn't miss
your open house.

01:00.260 --> 01:03.127
You kids are the most important thing
in our lives.

01:03.229 --> 01:04.821
Oh, my God! We forgot Meg.

01:04.931 --> 01:07.525
Don't worry about Meg. She's got
everything she needs in her room.

01:20.280 --> 01:23.113
Most of the time,
the kids'll exercise out in the field.

01:23.249 --> 01:27.117
But if it's raining or I'm hung-over,
they stay inside and play dodge ball.

01:27.220 --> 01:29.620
I love dodge ball! Heads up!

01:31.691 --> 01:33.989
And this week in Home Ec,
we're teaching your kids...

01:34.094 --> 01:35.254
how to make bundt cake.

01:35.361 --> 01:37.556
I love bundt cake! Heads up!

01:39.732 --> 01:42.292
The school band offers a wide variety
of instruments...

01:42.402 --> 01:43.994
from the kettledrum to the trombone.

01:44.104 --> 01:45.833
I love the trombone!

01:47.474 --> 01:49.032
[Playing soulful tune]

01:59.452 --> 02:00.510
Wow!

02:00.854 --> 02:03.880
I know, isn't he wonderful?
He took lessons in junior college.

02:03.990 --> 02:05.048
Heads up!

02:07.927 --> 02:10.896
I like meeting Chris's teachers.
This ought to be more interesting than...

02:10.997 --> 02:12.692
that time I met Ted Danson.

02:12.899 --> 02:15.663
Wow! Ted Danson and Mary Steenburgen!

02:15.768 --> 02:17.702
Always nice to meet a fan.

02:19.005 --> 02:20.905
Oh, shoot! I forgot my umbrella.

02:21.007 --> 02:22.668
That's okay, honey. Come on over here.

02:22.775 --> 02:23.764
Thanks, dear.

02:23.877 --> 02:27.369
Sometimes it's good to be a freak.
Do you want to sleep together later?

02:27.480 --> 02:32.281
No. Thanks, though.

02:32.552 --> 02:35.953
Good evening, parents. I'm Ms. Clifton.
I'd like for you to fill out these...

02:36.055 --> 02:39.252
contact information sheets.
Now, who would like to pass them out?

02:40.560 --> 02:42.460
Ms. Clifton, over here!

02:42.962 --> 02:46.591
Ms. Clifton! Ms. Clifton! Ms. Clifton!
Ms. Clifton! Ms. Clifton!

02:52.739 --> 02:54.172
Mrs. Griffin.

02:55.975 --> 02:59.035
I'm sorry. Will you all please excuse me
for a moment?

02:59.279 --> 03:01.110
<i>MAN: [On TV] Tonight's winning
lottery numbers are...</i>

03:01.214 --> 03:04.809
<i>6, 21, 18, 7, 42.</i>

03:05.585 --> 03:08.281
Oh, my God! I won!

03:08.388 --> 03:11.915
I'm free from all those
snot-nosed, little bastards!

03:13.626 --> 03:15.116
I'm free!

03:15.228 --> 03:17.196
[Ms. Clifton laughing maniacally]

03:18.898 --> 03:21.093
- Is she coming back?
- I don't know.

03:21.801 --> 03:22.995
[Audience laughing]

03:27.874 --> 03:32.004
I can't believe Ms. Clifton's gone.
Who's gonna teach my class now?

03:32.111 --> 03:34.602
Brian, why don't you teach Chris's class?

03:34.714 --> 03:37.512
You're very knowledgeable, the kids
might knock you down a few pegs...

03:37.617 --> 03:38.606
which would be good for you.

03:38.718 --> 03:42.620
You know, that is a terrific idea, Lois.
I probably have a lot to offer young people.

03:42.722 --> 03:43.848
What's he going to teach them?

03:43.957 --> 03:46.983
How to lick the Dorito crumbs
from between the sofa cushions?

03:47.093 --> 03:48.754
Or how to leave a dead bird on the carpet?

03:48.861 --> 03:50.522
That was a gift, you bastard.

03:50.630 --> 03:52.461
That was a gift for the family.

03:55.568 --> 03:58.696
Good morning, class.
I'm your substitute teacher, Brian Griffin.

03:58.871 --> 04:01.431
Good morning, Mr. Griffin.

04:02.041 --> 04:05.374
Please. Call me Brian.
Mr. Griffin is my father.

04:05.478 --> 04:09.710
I thought your father's name was Cocoa,
and he was hit by a milk truck!

04:09.816 --> 04:12.717
All right. Our goal here is to gain
a command of the English language.

04:12.819 --> 04:16.152
So you can be successful writers
like Ben Affleck and Matt Damon.

04:16.856 --> 04:20.724
<i>There. Finished.
Good Will Hunting by Matt Damon.</i>

04:20.927 --> 04:23.259
You think we could put
both our names on that?

04:23.363 --> 04:26.127
What? You've done nothing
but eat Breyer's and smoke pot...

04:26.232 --> 04:27.460
for the last six months.

04:27.567 --> 04:30.195
Oh, that's... Come on! I helped.

04:30.303 --> 04:33.431
Oh, yeah? Okay, write a line.
Just right now.

04:33.539 --> 04:35.063
- Just pitch me a line right now.
- Okay.

04:35.174 --> 04:36.141
[Farts]

04:36.242 --> 04:37.266
How about that?

04:37.377 --> 04:40.505
- That wasn't a line. You just farted.
- Is there anymore pot?

04:43.950 --> 04:47.909
So, how was your first day, Mr. Kotter?

04:48.788 --> 04:51.052
Yeah, Chris.
What's it like to have Brian as a teacher?

04:51.157 --> 04:55.116
It sucks! Mr. Griffin gave me an F
on my first assignment!

04:55.228 --> 04:58.493
What? An F, Brian?
After all Chris has done for you?

04:58.865 --> 05:01.993
Yeah. Just kind of pull it out. Yeah.

05:02.935 --> 05:05.597
If dogs aren't supposed to eat
dental floss out of the garbage...

05:05.705 --> 05:07.172
why do they make it mint-flavored?

05:07.507 --> 05:10.135
Chris, when I was in school,
you know what we used to do...

05:10.243 --> 05:11.471
when a teacher gave us a bad grade?

05:11.577 --> 05:13.238
- What?
- We'd egg his house.

05:13.346 --> 05:15.974
- Come on. Where's this bastard live?
- I'll show you.

05:17.583 --> 05:18.709
That's his house!

05:20.720 --> 05:21.880
- Take that!
- I got it!

05:21.988 --> 05:23.182
Take that, you bum!

05:23.356 --> 05:24.414
What the hell are you doing?

05:24.524 --> 05:25.786
- Is that him?
- Yeah!

05:25.892 --> 05:26.859
Oh, crap!

05:30.530 --> 05:34.159
[In Southern accent] Hello, class.
Mark Twain here, filling in for Brian Griffin.

05:34.300 --> 05:38.327
<i>I understand you children read my book,
The Adventures of Huckleberry Finn.</i>

05:38.438 --> 05:39.735
Yeah, we read it.

05:39.839 --> 05:42.364
Now, who can tell me...
Bobby, stop screwing around back there!

05:42.475 --> 05:45.911
Who can tell me the significance of
the carpetbaggers in my novel?

05:46.012 --> 05:47.980
Yeah. They stood for corruption and greed.

05:48.081 --> 05:52.313
That's exactly right.
Just like the presidency of James Garfield.

05:53.820 --> 05:54.980
He died in office.

05:55.088 --> 05:58.888
You kids are mighty smart.
You must have a powerful good teacher.

05:59.025 --> 06:02.961
Well, I gotta catch my time steamboat
back to the 1800s.

06:07.066 --> 06:11.025
- Sorry I'm late. Did I miss anything?
- Yeah! Cap'n Crunch was here.

06:11.137 --> 06:13.230
Didn't you pass him on the stairs?

06:13.339 --> 06:16.035
Well, I hope the rest of you kids
learned something today.

06:16.142 --> 06:17.632
Yeah.

06:17.744 --> 06:19.905
<i>[Over P.A. system] Good morning,
this is Principal Sloan.</i>

06:20.012 --> 06:21.172
<i>Mr. Griffin, you've been reassigned.</i>

06:21.280 --> 06:22.804
<i>Please report to Remedial English.</i>

06:22.915 --> 06:26.544
Reassigned? Can I at least come down
to your office and talk to you about this?

06:26.652 --> 06:29.883
No. I'm afraid I'm far too busy today.

06:29.989 --> 06:33.220
<i>Estoban, mucho tension lower.</i>

06:33.960 --> 06:36.895
Little lower. Lower.

06:37.530 --> 06:40.158
Lower.

06:40.266 --> 06:42.791
<i>[Singing in shrill voice] On top of
old Smokey</i>

06:43.236 --> 06:45.500
Gosh, I was really starting to like this job.

06:45.605 --> 06:47.766
It was nice interacting with
intelligent people.

06:47.874 --> 06:49.102
I usually hang out with an idiot.

06:50.276 --> 06:52.938
Brian, check it out.
I made a water slide in the house.

06:57.784 --> 06:59.479
[Groaning in pain]

07:02.054 --> 07:06.286
I'm not gonna call the hospital
because you won't learn anything if I do.

07:06.626 --> 07:08.924
Well, kids, I'll see you later.

07:10.329 --> 07:13.059
Pardon me. Is this first-period English?

07:14.534 --> 07:17.059
I'm your new teacher, Mrs. Lockhart.

07:21.974 --> 07:24.772
Oh, my God. I'm in love.

07:24.877 --> 07:26.845
Watch out for the stairs!

07:27.113 --> 07:28.740
[Crashing]

07:36.222 --> 07:40.283
- Good morning, class.
- Good morning, Mrs. Lockhart.

07:40.393 --> 07:43.851
I graded your quizzes from yesterday.
Most of you did well.

07:44.063 --> 07:48.124
Some of you, I think, can do better.
What do you see here, Chris?

07:50.236 --> 07:51.703
Two D's and an F.

07:57.276 --> 07:59.073
[Funky instrumental music playing]

08:02.148 --> 08:05.948
Hi. I'm Mr. Griffin.
But you can call me Brian.

08:06.219 --> 08:07.686
Mr. Griffin is my father.

08:07.787 --> 08:08.811
[Gunshot]

08:08.921 --> 08:11.856
<i>Well, has anybody read Huckleberry Finn?</i>

08:12.191 --> 08:15.217
All right. How about we go around
the room and everyone can say...

08:15.328 --> 08:16.955
a little something about themselves?

08:17.063 --> 08:18.428
Let's start with you there in the front.

08:18.531 --> 08:20.999
My name's Tim. I'm 28 years young.

08:21.100 --> 08:22.328
And I love weed.

08:22.435 --> 08:27.338
My name is Carlos. And beneath
my tough exterior is a boy aching to learn.

08:27.707 --> 08:29.470
And beneath that is a rapist.

08:29.575 --> 08:32.339
My name is Amanda.
And my water just broke.

08:32.445 --> 08:34.572
- Oh, my God!
- Yo, it's my turn to deliver.

08:34.680 --> 08:37.877
Can I have this one?
My mom keeps giving mine away.

08:40.586 --> 08:44.317
Dad, I need some advice. I need to know
how to get a girl to like me.

08:44.423 --> 08:46.755
Chris, buddy, there's a million ways
to do that.

08:46.859 --> 08:49.054
You just got to do something simple,
like Vincent van Gogh.

08:49.428 --> 08:51.953
It's... What is this?

08:52.064 --> 08:53.929
It's my ear. Do you like it?

08:54.500 --> 08:55.592
You don't like it.

08:55.701 --> 08:58.898
No, I like it. But it's just... Why your ear?

08:59.005 --> 09:00.131
Because I love you.

09:00.239 --> 09:03.402
Well, at least this will be a funny story
to tell our kids someday.

09:03.509 --> 09:06.569
You want kids? Oh, yikes.

09:08.080 --> 09:10.776
I wish you'd told me that
before I got you this.

09:11.617 --> 09:15.280
Did I hear my big boy say he's got
a crush on some lucky girl?

09:15.388 --> 09:18.789
You know, Chris, I knew this day
would come. So, I brought you a condom.

09:18.891 --> 09:21.052
Use it wisely, though.
It wasn't easy to obtain.

09:21.394 --> 09:22.861
[Man and woman moaning]

09:24.597 --> 09:26.121
MAN: What the hell are you doing?

09:26.232 --> 09:28.928
WOMAN: Give that back!
MAN: Man!

09:29.035 --> 09:32.436
WOMAN: Now, where were we?
MAN: This is much better.

09:32.872 --> 09:36.808
Chris, honey, the way to win a girl is
to do something romantic and unexpected.

09:37.410 --> 09:39.537
Remember the naked spaceman, Lois?

09:39.645 --> 09:42.512
Yeah. You remember the naked spaceman.

09:43.816 --> 09:46.649
On my 25th birthday,
your father surprised me by showing up...

09:46.752 --> 09:49.482
in nothing but a space helmet
and moon boots.

09:50.222 --> 09:51.450
It just came to me.

09:52.325 --> 09:56.421
- You want some Tang, Mr. Spaceman?
- Do I?

09:58.331 --> 10:01.994
Just remember, fat man,
those jugs are mine until the milk dries up.

10:02.301 --> 10:04.292
Then you can have the remains.

10:06.906 --> 10:11.741
So, basically, what Orwell was saying
was, "It's not perfect but I'll take it."

10:12.044 --> 10:13.341
All right, moving on...

10:13.446 --> 10:15.414
CHRIS: Sorry, I'm late, Mrs. Lockhart.

10:15.514 --> 10:18.278
Oh, my God, Chris! What are you doing?

10:18.384 --> 10:20.614
Being romantic and unexpected.

10:20.786 --> 10:22.777
Chris, you can't be so impulsive.

10:22.888 --> 10:24.879
People have gotten
into a lot of trouble that way.

10:27.560 --> 10:29.653
- Marie?
- Yeah, Donny?

10:32.031 --> 10:33.760
We cannot tell Mom.

10:36.836 --> 10:39.805
So, Chris, what's the latest with
your little girlfriend?

10:39.905 --> 10:43.306
I don't think Mrs. Lockhart likes me at all.

10:43.442 --> 10:45.842
Mrs. Lockhart? Your teacher?

10:46.045 --> 10:47.535
Whoa!

10:47.680 --> 10:49.671
Whoa! Whoa! Whoa! Whoa!

10:52.418 --> 10:54.283
Lois, this is not my Batman glass.

10:54.420 --> 10:57.014
Peter, are you listening?
Chris has a crush on his teacher.

10:57.123 --> 10:58.385
Gross!

10:58.491 --> 10:59.788
You know what else is gross?

10:59.892 --> 11:00.881
[Farts]

11:00.993 --> 11:03.018
Broke a damn blood vessel!

11:06.766 --> 11:08.290
How's it coming, dog?

11:08.401 --> 11:11.529
<i>God! Just listen to this kid's report
on Great Expectations.</i>

11:11.637 --> 11:15.266
"Miss Havisham should have throwed
that cake out so it don't like...

11:15.374 --> 11:17.569
"mess all up the bitch's house."

11:17.677 --> 11:21.613
I don't know what to do, you know?
Society's given up on these kids.

11:21.714 --> 11:23.614
I feel like I may be the only one
who can help them.

11:23.716 --> 11:26.116
I think your problem is
you're not communicating in a way...

11:26.218 --> 11:27.378
that speaks to their experience.

11:27.486 --> 11:28.714
You know what you should do?

11:28.821 --> 11:30.812
Get in there tomorrow and do the robot.

11:35.127 --> 11:37.322
Wow. You know, you're right.
Maybe I should just try...

11:37.430 --> 11:39.421
a whole new approach. Thanks.

11:39.665 --> 11:41.758
[Funky music playing on stereo]

11:42.068 --> 11:43.535
Okay, you can stop that now.

11:43.636 --> 11:45.263
I can't hear you. I'm a robot.

11:45.371 --> 11:47.635
- Come on, knock it off.
- Does not compute.

11:49.041 --> 11:51.874
- I'm going to bed.
- I do not require sleep.

11:55.314 --> 11:57.976
<i>Let's see the kid with the hearing aid
from Barney do this.</i>

12:01.187 --> 12:05.089
All right. So's I'm chilling in Verona
when my homie busts out with:

12:05.191 --> 12:08.991
"Yo, Romeo. Check out
that biotch Juliet in the window."

12:09.128 --> 12:11.596
Problem is, Juliet's peeps are, like,
East Coast rappers...

12:11.697 --> 12:14.689
and my posse's representing West Side.

12:14.800 --> 12:17.894
Just like my boys Tupac and Biggie.
Know what I'm saying?

12:18.170 --> 12:21.162
- That's racist, man.
- Yeah, that's just straight ignorant, dog.

12:23.075 --> 12:25.236
It's good to meet you, Mr. and Mrs. Griffin.

12:25.344 --> 12:28.370
We wanted to talk to you about
our son. You see, Chris really...

12:28.481 --> 12:32.144
Lois, honey, let's make sure
we do this delicately, all right?

12:32.251 --> 12:35.277
Mrs. Lockhart, our son...

12:35.721 --> 12:38.656
would like to plow you.

12:39.725 --> 12:42.421
I had a feeling that's what was going on.

12:42.528 --> 12:45.725
Sorry. Our son can sometimes be a boob.
I mean a melon.

12:45.831 --> 12:50.461
I mean, a sopping-wet pair of breasts
barely covered by a racing t-shirt.

12:50.569 --> 12:52.469
Mrs. Lockhart,
we just wanted you to know...

12:52.571 --> 12:55.199
so you could spare his feelings
and let him down gently.

12:55.307 --> 12:58.105
Don't worry.
I know exactly what to say to Chris.

12:58.210 --> 13:01.407
Thank you so much.
You've been very understanding.

13:03.249 --> 13:06.946
Gosh. You know, I don't mean to impose,
but do you have a picture of yourself...

13:07.052 --> 13:09.111
that I could tape
to the back of Lois's head?

13:12.925 --> 13:14.119
[Rapping on window]

13:17.329 --> 13:19.991
- Mrs. Lockhart?
- Chris, come down here.

13:20.099 --> 13:21.964
I need to talk to you.

13:22.134 --> 13:23.362
Why are you here?

13:23.469 --> 13:26.370
'Cause I couldn't stand to be away
from you for another moment.

13:26.472 --> 13:29.032
I think I'm falling in love with you.

13:29.141 --> 13:32.440
- I love you, too!
- The only problem is I'm married.

13:32.878 --> 13:34.539
Therefore, there's only one thing to do.

13:36.415 --> 13:40.579
Make a flip book of a stick figure
whose head gets bigger and bigger...

13:40.686 --> 13:42.313
and bigger and then pops?

13:44.023 --> 13:47.151
This isn't a flip book, Chris.
They're instructions.

13:47.259 --> 13:51.389
If we're going to be together,
I need you to kill my husband.

13:53.799 --> 13:56.029
Do you have any idea what time it is?

13:56.135 --> 13:57.500
Get in the house, fatty!

14:05.845 --> 14:10.214
Chris, you big beautiful man,
I'm so glad you came.

14:11.250 --> 14:14.583
Up the stairs, second door on the left.
He should still be asleep.

14:14.720 --> 14:17.985
- Mrs. Lockhart, I don't think I can do this.
- What?

14:18.090 --> 14:20.888
Maybe you could just get a divorce,
and we could live together...

14:20.993 --> 14:22.358
in the fort under my bed.

14:22.461 --> 14:25.487
Fine. I'll do it myself. But we're through.

14:25.598 --> 14:29.125
Okay. But I got to give you the password,
or you can't get into the fort.

14:29.235 --> 14:30.259
[Door bangs shut]

14:30.369 --> 14:32.234
It's taco. Taco!

14:35.441 --> 14:37.739
Good God!
Look at the fat man's underwear.

14:37.843 --> 14:41.176
It looks like a Jackson Pollock painting.
Don't put that in with my things!

14:41.280 --> 14:42.542
What's this?

14:42.648 --> 14:46.345
You know, Stewie, Mommy doesn't
usually read things out of Chris's pockets.

14:46.452 --> 14:47.942
She's more respectful than that.

14:48.053 --> 14:50.385
Yeah, whatever helps you
sleep at night, bitch.

14:50.489 --> 14:52.821
Oh, my God!

14:52.925 --> 14:55.393
Chris is gonna murder
Mrs. Lockhart's husband!

14:55.494 --> 14:57.121
We got to stop him!

14:57.329 --> 15:01.356
Can we stop at the supermarket?
I want a Granny Smith apple.

15:05.037 --> 15:06.902
How's your oatmeal, honey?

15:07.006 --> 15:09.736
You know,
it tastes kind of different than usual.

15:10.809 --> 15:13.539
Oh, my God! There's a bear in my oatmeal.

15:14.847 --> 15:16.542
[Mr. Lockhart screaming]

15:16.782 --> 15:18.249
[Bear growling]

15:24.323 --> 15:27.690
Yeah, I know. I'm late.
Okay, let's just get started.

15:32.898 --> 15:35.731
Yo, man, what's that thing in the middle?

15:36.168 --> 15:39.296
What, this?
You got to be freaking kidding me.

15:39.471 --> 15:42.531
That's an ampersand.
It's a symbol for the word "and."

15:42.675 --> 15:46.372
My God, nobody can be this stupid.
Not even Peter when he took...

15:46.478 --> 15:48.742
<i>that blow to the head and thought he was
Larry from Three's Company.</i>

15:49.114 --> 15:51.912
Jack, there's a hot tub party
across the street and we're invited.

15:52.017 --> 15:56.010
And don't worry. If Mr. Furley comes by,
I'll make sure he thinks you're...

15:56.588 --> 16:00.217
Mr. Griffin, chillax.
We're doing the best we can.

16:00.326 --> 16:03.386
There is nothing I would like to do
more than chillax, Amanda.

16:03.495 --> 16:06.589
But without a decent education,
you could spend the rest of your life...

16:06.699 --> 16:08.826
as a ditch digger or a motel maid
or a hooker.

16:08.934 --> 16:11.494
- I could be a ditch digger?
- A motel maid?

16:11.603 --> 16:12.763
I could be a hooker?

16:12.871 --> 16:14.930
Well, no. You don't want to be a hooker.

16:15.040 --> 16:18.601
Wow, Mr. Griffin! You're the first teacher
that ever told us we could do anything.

16:18.711 --> 16:21.339
Well, I didn't mean sell your body
for money.

16:21.747 --> 16:23.305
"O, Captain! my Captain!"

16:23.415 --> 16:24.677
No, you're actually misunderstanding.

16:24.783 --> 16:25.909
"O, Captain! my Captain!"

16:26.018 --> 16:27.349
Well, if it works for you, I guess...

16:27.453 --> 16:28.920
"O, Captain! my Captain!"

16:29.021 --> 16:30.886
What the hell?
Be the best damn hooker you can be.

16:30.990 --> 16:32.548
"O, Captain! my Captain!"

16:32.658 --> 16:34.649
In your case, I'd get the money up front.

16:36.628 --> 16:37.993
[Groaning]

16:40.099 --> 16:43.557
Jack, twins! Swedish. My place. Now.

16:47.906 --> 16:50.466
We're too late! Oh, my God.

16:51.210 --> 16:52.677
Okay, I gotta call the police.

16:53.779 --> 16:55.337
What's that smell?

16:55.447 --> 16:57.608
Dead body, right. That's what that is.

16:57.950 --> 17:02.011
I just had a dream I was an egg, and I was
being hatched by Elisabeth Hasselbeck.

17:03.155 --> 17:05.851
No, wait a minute. I can't call the police.

17:05.958 --> 17:08.620
I have to get rid of this body,
or Chris'll go to prison!

17:08.727 --> 17:12.185
<i>And we all know what happens in those
prison showers. I've seen Oz.</i>

17:12.464 --> 17:14.455
<i>[Singing]Scrub scrub here,
scrub scrub there</i>

17:14.566 --> 17:16.033
<i>Whether you're white or bronze</i>

17:16.135 --> 17:20.071
<i>A man can wash another man
in the merry old land of Oz</i>

17:25.811 --> 17:29.474
All right, wait here, Stewie,
while Mommy gets the cement blocks.

17:34.386 --> 17:37.844
- Everything all right here?
- Fine, Officer. Just enjoying the sunset.

17:37.956 --> 17:39.924
No law against that, is there?

17:40.025 --> 17:44.052
- What happened to your shirt?
- You know, just a pizza party at the office.

17:44.163 --> 17:45.528
Yeah? Where do you work?

17:45.631 --> 17:48.065
First Fidelity Insurance
over on Wabossette Street.

17:48.167 --> 17:51.364
- My cousin, Arnie, works over there.
- Arnie's your cousin, is he?

17:51.470 --> 17:52.835
- You know him?
- Somewhat.

17:52.938 --> 17:55.805
Good middle-management type.
Just blends in with the furniture there.

17:55.908 --> 17:57.739
Never really wowed anyone at the office.

17:57.843 --> 18:00.937
Yeah, that's always been Arnie's problem.
Well, take it easy.

18:01.046 --> 18:04.209
Yes. You, too.
And if you see Arnie, tell him:

18:04.316 --> 18:05.305
[Gibbering]

18:05.417 --> 18:06.884
He'll know what it means.

18:13.358 --> 18:16.088
You know what I hate?
A guy in a blue suit.

18:16.195 --> 18:17.560
[Exclaims]

18:17.663 --> 18:20.632
There's one right behind me, isn't there?

18:22.301 --> 18:26.260
You know, Lois, Chris is cool and
everything, but since he killed that guy...

18:26.371 --> 18:28.464
I don't know. Maybe he shouldn't be
living with us here now.

18:28.574 --> 18:29.563
Peter, I'm scared.

18:29.675 --> 18:32.303
Don't worry, sweetheart.
You'll have plenty of time to escape...

18:32.411 --> 18:35.039
while he's killing Meg.
He hates her the most.

18:35.147 --> 18:38.310
Hey, everybody. What's for dinner?
I'm starving.

18:38.417 --> 18:41.147
My God, his blood lust is unquenchable!

18:41.253 --> 18:44.017
Chris, why don't you take your sister
into the kitchen for a sandwich?

18:44.123 --> 18:45.784
I don't want to die!

18:46.225 --> 18:48.352
Why is everybody acting weird?

18:48.460 --> 18:50.087
Chris, honey, we know what you did.

18:50.195 --> 18:52.823
And I have to say,
honestly, I don't approve.

18:52.931 --> 18:57.630
What I did? That I lied about my age
to get into Indian Bingo?

18:57.736 --> 18:59.294
No.

18:59.404 --> 19:01.895
That I had hard gas and pooed myself?

19:02.007 --> 19:03.099
Close, but still no.

19:03.208 --> 19:04.197
How is that close?

19:04.309 --> 19:06.709
For God's sake, Chris!
You murdered Mr. Lockhart!

19:06.812 --> 19:08.279
What? No, I didn't!

19:08.380 --> 19:10.940
Come on. Everybody's done
something they're not proud of.

19:11.049 --> 19:12.482
Like when I used to be a Wonder Twin.

19:12.584 --> 19:15.553
Peter, the old schoolhouse is on fire!
Let's go!

19:15.687 --> 19:17.655
Wonder Twin powers, activate!

19:17.756 --> 19:19.280
Form of a hawk!

19:20.359 --> 19:23.055
- Come on, Peter.
- Yeah, I'll be right behind you.

19:24.129 --> 19:27.360
Shape of Jayna's tampon.

19:31.236 --> 19:34.171
PETER: And now I play the waiting game.

19:34.540 --> 19:36.007
Chris, I saw the body.

19:36.108 --> 19:39.942
Premeditated murder is one thing,
but I will not have lying in this house.

19:40.045 --> 19:43.014
<i>Wait, hold it.
Can we finish this after Joan of Arcadia?</i>

19:43.115 --> 19:44.707
<i>Is Joan of Arcadia on?</i>

19:44.883 --> 19:46.009
All right.

19:46.118 --> 19:47.210
Must be good.

19:47.319 --> 19:48.308
Enjoyable program.

19:48.420 --> 19:51.389
<i>We interrupt this broadcast
to bring you a breaking news story.</i>

19:51.490 --> 19:54.550
<i>We apologize to Joan of Arcadia's
sanctimonious, fear-based...</i>

19:54.660 --> 19:56.389
<i>and probably overweight viewers.</i>

19:56.495 --> 19:58.793
That's right, Diane.
It appears Ronald Lockhart...

19:58.897 --> 20:02.025
has been brutally murdered by his wife,
Lana, and a local bear.

20:02.367 --> 20:06.303
Well, I'll be damned.
Chris, I guess we owe you an apology.

20:06.405 --> 20:10.535
That's okay. I just wonder what happened
to Ms. Lockhart and that bear.

20:10.709 --> 20:12.939
The whereabouts of these suspects
are currently unknown.

20:14.846 --> 20:16.814
- You ready?
- What's that?

20:17.015 --> 20:19.711
I thought we'd try that lobster place
we passed in the car.

20:19.818 --> 20:24.221
- Yeah, can I just finish watching this?
- You can watch TV anytime. I'm starving.

20:24.323 --> 20:28.157
Lana, this is gonna be a real long trip
if you don't knock off the crap!

20:30.362 --> 20:31.920
Love you.

20:31.921 --> 21:32.921
Thank you for watching «Family Guy» on
www.FOX-fan.ru